# `az acr build` tars and uploads the ENTIRE folder (git-ignored files included)
# before building. The .env exclusions below keep live credentials off the build
# agents; the rest just shrinks the upload.

# secrets — never upload
**/.env
**/.env.*
!backend/.env.local.example

# NOTE: the old az CLI on this machine (used by deploy.ps1) has a buggy
# .dockerignore matcher: `dir/` trailing-slash patterns are NOT honored when it
# packs the upload tar (verified 2026-07-03 — db/ and node_modules went up).
# Every directory is therefore listed BOTH bare and with /** so both the local
# az packer and the real Docker daemon exclude it. Verify any change with the
# pack_check repro (see CLAUDE.md deployment section).

# heavy / rebuilt in-image
backend/.venv
backend/.venv/**
backend/static
backend/static/**
frontend/node_modules
frontend/node_modules/**
frontend/dist
frontend/dist/**

# caches & test artifacts
**/__pycache__
**/__pycache__/**
**/*.pyc
backend/.pytest_cache
backend/.pytest_cache/**
backend/.ruff_cache
backend/.ruff_cache/**
backend/.coverage
backend/tests
backend/tests/**
backend/scripts
backend/scripts/**

# not needed in the image (db/ holds the real-data baseline export — NEVER upload)
db
db/**
docs
docs/**
infra
infra/**
*.md
**/*.md
CLAUDE.md
# EXCEPTION: backend/prompts/*.md are runtime-loaded system prompts (load_prompt in
# services/prompts.py reads /app/prompts/<kind>.md), NOT docs — re-include them despite
# the blanket *.md exclusion above (later rules win). Listed bare AND with /** for the
# old az CLI's buggy dir matcher, same convention as the exclusions above. The Dockerfile
# must also `COPY backend/prompts ./prompts` — .dockerignore only controls the upload.
!backend/prompts
!backend/prompts/**
.claude
.claude/**
.gitignore
deploy.ps1
